    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Heat the oil in a wok or wide pan over medium-high heat. Sauté the garlic and onion until soft and fragrant.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the pork and stir-fry until it renders some fat and loses its pink color. Add the chicken and cook until opaque.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Pour in 1 cup of the broth and the soy sauce. Cover and simmer until the pork is tender.",
        "minutes": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the shrimp, carrot and snow peas and cook just until the shrimp turn pink. Scoop out most of the meat, shrimp and vegetables with a slotted spoon and set aside, leaving the liquid in the pan.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the remaining broth, the oyster sauce and the pepper and bring to a boil.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the noodles and toss with tongs as they soften, until they have absorbed almost all the liquid. Add a splash of water if they are still firm when the pan is dry.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Return the meat, shrimp and vegetables with the cabbage and celery. Toss until the cabbage just wilts.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Taste and adjust with soy sauce. Serve hot with calamansi on the side.",
        "minutes": null
      }
    ],
    "tips": "Pull the vegetables out before the noodles go in so they stay crisp. If you cook ahead for a party, stop when the noodles are slightly firm: they keep softening as they sit."
